          "tz": -240
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-09-10 04:50:28.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20714 lov: bound foreign LOV EA reads by buffer size",
        "message": "LU-20714 lov: bound foreign LOV EA reads by buffer size\n\nThe foreign layout EA reaches the client as a reply buffer of\nmbo_eadatasize bytes, and its readers trust it. ll_manage_foreign()\nchecks only that the length is non-zero before reading lfm_magic and\nlfm_type, and lsme_unpack_foreign() reads both before it bounds\nlfm_length, so a buffer shorter than the 16-byte lov_foreign_md\nheader is read past its end. lsm_unpackmd_foreign() never compares\nlfm_length with buf_size at all, then memcpy()s that many bytes out,\nand readlink() or lfs getstripe hands the result to userspace.\n\nBound all three reads by the buffer the EA arrived in.\nlod_verify_striping() bounds a foreign layout when it is set, so\nreaching any of them needs a corrupt on-disk EA or a hostile MDS.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 6a20bdcc608b (\"LU-11376 lov: new foreign LOV format\")\nFixes: 15d44e787e17 (\"LU-12682 llite: fake symlink type of foreign file/dir\")\nFixes: 61a002cd8631 (\"LU-13602 flr: skip unknown FLR component types\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Id7acfb24dd190da63cf9ced7ae22d28da1874e37\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
